# Signed release files are hashed BYTE FOR BYTE. If Git converted line endings
# (CRLF on Windows, LF on Linux), a checkout on another OS would no longer match
# the signed manifest and release_A would fail with HASH_MISMATCH / BAD_SIGNATURE.
# "-text" tells Git to store and check out these files exactly as they are.
release_A/** -text
*.sig binary
*.pem -text
